  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A part of a complete circuit is shown in the figure. At some instant, the value of current I is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and it is decreasing at a rate of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>As</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of the potential difference&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></math> (in volts) at that instant is-</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0125_44ead061e351.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 95px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "33",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>L</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>33</mn></math></p>"
